[36m(TaskRunner pid=481996)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=481996)[0m We need to find the divisors of \(362880\) that have units digit 1, i.e., divisors \(d\) such that \(d \equiv 1 \pmod{10}\). This implies \(d \equiv 1 \pmod{2}\) and \(d \equiv 1 \pmod{5}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=481996)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=481996)[0m Since \(d \equiv 1 \pmod{2}\), \(d\) must be odd. This implies the exponent of 2 in the prime factorization must be 0. 
